          %h2#references References
          %p On quantum effect operators:
          %ul
            %li#Ludwig
              %p
                G. Ludwig,
                %em Foundations of Quantum Mechanics I
                Springer Verlag, New York, (1983)
            %li#Kraus
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karl+Kraus"}> Karl Kraus
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em States, Effects, and Operations – Fundamental Notions of Quantum Theory
                %strong 190
                Springer (1983) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-12732-1"}> doi:10.1007/3-540-12732-1
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Teiko+Heinosaari"}> Teiko Heinosaari
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M%C3%A1rio+Ziman"} Mário Ziman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Mathematical Language of Quantum Theory – From Uncertainty to Entanglement
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139031103"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139031103
          %p The notion of effect algebra is due to
          %ul#FoulisBennet
            %li
              D. J. Foulis, M. K. Bennet,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Effect algebras and unsharp quantum logics
          %p
            Discussion of effect algebras in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+logic"} categorical logic
            is in
          %ul#Jacobs
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bart+Jacobs"}> Bart Jacobs
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em New Directions in Categorical Logic, for Classical, Probabilistic and Quantum Logic
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1205.3940"} arXiv:1205.3940
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+logic"} quantum logic
            is in section 6 of
          %ul
            %li
              Gianpiero Cattaneo, Maria Luisa Dalla Chiara, Roberto Giuntini and Francesco Paoli,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum Logic and Nonclassical Logics
              = succeed "," do
                %em Handbook of Quantum Logic and Quantum Structures: Quantum Logic
          %p
            A survey of the use of effect algebras in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Teiko Heinosaari, Mario Ziman,
                %em Guide to Mathematical Concepts of Quantum Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0810.3536"}> arXiv:0810.3536
                )
              %p also appeared as:
              %p
                %em> The Mathematical Language of Quantum Theory
                , Cambridge University Press (2011)
            %li
              %p
                Hans de Groote,
                %em On a canonical lattice structure on the effect algebra of a von Neumann algebra
                %a#DeGroote{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0410018"} arXiv:0410018
          %p
            Discussion in relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^{op}
            (hence in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
            for objects) and density of Boolean algebras is in
          %ul
            %li
              Sam Staton, Sander Uijlen,
              %em Effect algebras, presheaves, non-locality and contextuality
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.cs.ru.nl/S.Uijlen/ICALP-camera-ready.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p D-posets were first introduced in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                F. Kôpka,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em D-posets of fuzzy sets
            %li
              %p
                F. Chovanec and F. Kôpka,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em D-lattices
